From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:37:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 080/138] wifi: brcmfmac: pcie: Keep the function in D0 across
 system suspend

LOCAL (Hoolock, T7000). The mainline suspend path sends D3_INFORM and
lets the PCI core put the BCM4345 into D3hot, which moves the link into
PCI-PM L1 and needs a config write to come back. The n61 root port runs
with ASPM off because iOS cannot touch config space in L1/L2
(acpie-l1ss-workaround); whether this root complex survives the D3hot
round trip is unknown, and a bus hang there means DFU.

By default, stay in D0: stop the console timer and save the config
space. A saved state keeps the PCI core from changing the power state of
the function and, through skip_bus_pm, of the root port, so the link
never leaves L0; on suspend-to-idle the noirq power-up is skipped and
pci_pm_resume() only writes the saved config back, still in L0.
cfg80211 has already disassociated and enabled MPC by then, so the
radio is off either way. Resume just restarts the console timer.

brcmfmac.pcie_d3=1 (0644) selects the original D3 handshake.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c        | 33 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index fb2e8d680..e47e11b51 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -365,6 +365,7 @@ struct brcmf_pciedev_info {
 	bool console_active;
 	struct timer_list timer;
 #endif
+	bool kept_d0;
 };
 
 struct brcmf_pcie_ringbuf {
@@ -2654,6 +2655,18 @@ brcmf_pcie_remove(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM
 
 
+/*
+ * LOCAL (Hoolock, T7000): by default the function stays in D0 across system
+ * suspend. The n61 root port runs without ASPM because iOS cannot touch config
+ * space while the link is in L1/L2 (acpie-l1ss-workaround), and D3hot puts the
+ * link into PCI-PM L1 with a config write on the way out. cfg80211 already
+ * disassociates and enables MPC before this runs, so the radio is off either
+ * way. pcie_d3=1 restores the D3 handshake (D3_INFORM + PCI core D3hot).
+ */
+static bool brcmf_pcie_d3;
+module_param_named(pcie_d3, brcmf_pcie_d3, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(pcie_d3, "Put the PCIe function into D3 on system suspend (default: keep it in D0)");
+
 static int brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo;
@@ -2665,6 +2678,20 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3(struct device *dev)
 	devinfo = bus->bus_priv.pcie->devinfo;
 
 	brcmf_pcie_fwcon_timer(devinfo, false);
+
+	devinfo->kept_d0 = !READ_ONCE(brcmf_pcie_d3);
+	if (devinfo->kept_d0) {
+		/*
+		 * Firmware and link stay as they are. With the config space
+		 * saved here the PCI core leaves this function and the root
+		 * port in D0 (no D3hot, so the link stays in L0); on resume
+		 * it only writes the saved config back, still in L0.
+		 */
+		pci_save_state(devinfo->pdev);
+		brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "staying in D0\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	brcmf_bus_change_state(bus, BRCMF_BUS_DOWN);
 
 	devinfo->mbdata_completed = false;
@@ -2697,6 +2724,12 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3(struct device *dev)
 	devinfo = bus->bus_priv.pcie->devinfo;
 	brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "Enter, dev=%p, bus=%p\n", dev, bus);
 
+	if (devinfo->kept_d0) {
+		devinfo->kept_d0 = false;
+		brcmf_pcie_fwcon_timer(devinfo, true);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	/* Check if device is still up and running, if so we are ready */
 	if (brcmf_pcie_read_reg32(devinfo, devinfo->reginfo->intmask) != 0) {
 		brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "Try to wakeup device....\n");
